From 990d2e42a60d97b0cfa624dec12af5c916a6b19a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 05:26:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/10] feat: load SpiralLoader mods at startup

The Director starts the mod loader right after configuration, before the
actor system, resources, or any server exist, then publishes lifecycle
events (ServerStarting, ServerResourcesLoaded, ServerStarted) on
ImlightModding.Events. Loader and mod log output goes through Imlight's
Logger. Behaviour is configured by the new [SpiralLoader] section of
Imlight.ini; with no mods installed Imlight behaves as before.

ImlightModding holds the attached event bus and registries. Until a loader
attaches, it exposes an inert bus, so call sites cost one interface call.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
